  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Banking Agents as Financial Inclusion Promoters in Underserved Areas</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Derechos humanos</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Colombia, exclusion from the financial system is particularly high in rural areas where nearly 37 percent of adults do not have access to any financial product, including a basic bank account. Where account access is available, 60 percent of savings accounts are inactive, indicating that the financial system is not designed to meet peoples needs. Banking agents, such as retail store or post office workers who serve as intermediaries for financial institutions, can help bring banking services to rural areas, but are typically expensive to select and train. To increase efficiencies for financial institutions working with banking agents, the implementing partner developed DIMO, a mobile platform that provides training modules, including standard onboarding topics, lessons on providing good customer service, and information about the financial institutions new products. DIMO is also a direct communication channel between the financial institutions and their banking agents, enabling financial institutions to share news, better serve their networks, and monitor agents through a dashboard. The implementing partner will enhance DIMO by developing, testing, and validating an alternative process that will speed up and reduce the costs of prospecting, selecting, and onboarding new banking agents. The implementing partner also plans to test and validate a new functionality that will enable banking agents to refer clients to financial institutions, thus facilitating their access to financial products. DIMO has the potential to leverage more than 50,000 micro and small businesses to extend banking agent networks that can help improve the lives of more than 11 million smallholder farmers, day laborers, microentrepreneurs, and informal employees in rural areas of Colombia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Protecci&#xf3;n avanzada de los derechos humanos internacionales, incluidos los derechos laborales, no cubiertos por otros elementos. Este elemento apoya a organizaciones gubernamentales y no gubernamentales creadas para proteger, promover y hacer cumplir los derechos humanos. Apoyar programas para educar a los gobiernos sobre la incorporaci&#xf3;n de normas y pr&#xe1;cticas de derechos humanos en todas las actividades gubernamentales.</narrative>
  </description>
